00:22:47.040 --> 00:23:06.420
And even though the whole thing is just that you just draw faster than, uh, the cowboy you're shooting, uh, targeted, you know, like you're in a duel with, even though that was the whole thing, because I was holding like, you know, their, their actual, uh, revolver and like having the, the arcade experience in front of me.

00:23:06.420 --> 00:23:14.020
I wound up doing that for way longer than I should have before realizing that like, yeah, like they're just not, they're not going to give me a reaction time I can't beat.

00:23:14.260 --> 00:23:35.580
Uh, so I think these games while simple still offer something to that like eighties arcade experience that like Freedom Force, Operation Wolf, Gotcha, are trying to do something, uh, you know, more innovative, uh, especially just with like getting out of the hit this target and move on space.

00:23:35.580 --> 00:23:36.760
Uh, and you'll see that a lot.

00:23:36.860 --> 00:23:44.660
Like you'll see, uh, on the Super Nintendo, on the Sega CD, on the, you know, like the Wii again, uh, we're talking about.

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:52.520
It's like, there's always going to be games that kind of just go back to, uh, yeah, it's just about hitting the targets and moving on to the next screen.

00:23:52.840 --> 00:23:57.420
I, uh, I do wonder like, where does the Zapper go from here?

00:23:57.680 --> 00:24:04.800
