00:32:14.080 --> 00:32:19.040
But that is, like, where, where Duck Hunt is, like, this arcade up your score experience.

00:32:19.320 --> 00:32:25.660
Uh, To the Earth feels like a, a proper, like, full video game where you're trying to beat the game.

00:32:25.900 --> 00:32:34.800
And it's hard because it's fast and, like, proves to me that the, that the, um, Zapper can be, like, this high, high, high octane, fast experience.

00:32:35.460 --> 00:32:44.860
And playing that back-to-back with Barker Bills really, really highlights how, like, Barker Bill kind of feels, I mean, forgive me, but feels a little bit like it's phoning it in.

00:32:45.020 --> 00:32:48.640
Where it's just like, yeah, we could do the Zapper thing, let's just throw some more things in there for them to shoot at.

00:32:48.740 --> 00:32:55.680
And when I'm playing this other game where I'm like, this is a very well-designed, like, high game design, very difficult game.

00:32:56.140 --> 00:33:01.580
Um, so overall, that, that also maybe tarnished my opinion of Barker Bill a little more.

00:33:01.580 --> 00:33:03.520
Um, so not essential.

00:33:03.640 --> 00:33:18.140
For what it's worth, I do think that whether it's short and simple or short and incredibly difficult, these kinds of peripheral-based or gimmicky, uh, video games do have a place to also be, um, incredibly entertaining, though.

00:33:18.140 --> 00:33:31.240
Like, I think about, uh, from an arcade experience, anytime I see House of the Dead or Time Crisis, uh, you know, like, even though I know I'm not gonna last long in those games, they're supposed to eat up your quarters.

00:33:31.240 --> 00:33:35.140
I feel compelled to just, like, you know, grab the gun and do some shooting.

00:33:35.140 --> 00:33:42.040
And, like, you know, I, I don't really evolve from the time I played it when I was 12 to the time I'm playing it now at Dave & Buster's.

00:33:42.200 --> 00:33:46.280
But, like, it's still fun to, to just have that short burst of excitement.

00:33:46.480 --> 00:33:53.780
And so I don't think that, like, again, that's why I was saying, like, we don't need a story mode, but we need something engaging on screen.

00:33:53.780 --> 00:34:04.220
