00:34:04.260 --> 00:34:07.660
Whereas, like, Wild Gunman, yeah, it's a duel, right?

00:34:07.680 --> 00:34:09.000
It's a completely different kind of thing.

00:34:09.000 --> 00:34:10.840
It's a duel. It's all about reaction time.

00:34:11.000 --> 00:34:17.800
Because the reaction time is just set to be, like, okay, this guy's five seconds, this guy's four seconds, whatever, right?

00:34:17.860 --> 00:34:20.680
It's, like, because they're just predetermined things, it gets kind of stale.

00:34:20.680 --> 00:34:24.600
No, it's not exciting enough, whereas, like, Duck Hunt always kept you on your toes.

00:34:24.660 --> 00:34:31.440
And I think that's kind of what you're saying about To The Earth, too, is, like, it's fast enough, it's difficult, but you can learn it.

00:34:31.720 --> 00:34:40.900
I feel like there is room for these games to not have to necessarily become traditional video games to wind up on the Essential Games list.

00:34:40.920 --> 00:34:42.440
